<node name="CDEP Prep Notes" unique_id="1" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="#0098a3" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h1" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">CDEP Prep Notes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Certified Detection Engineering Principal. This file holds your methodology, module notes and exam workspace as a tree of nodes. Pick a node on the left to open it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">The exam
</rich_text>
<rich_text>CDEP is a 10-day master-level exam. The breach is already contained. Your job is to build the detections that would have caught each stage, validate each one against the captured telemetry in your own resettable lab, and submit the value each validated rule returns as a flag. The commercial-grade report documents every analytic, mapped to MITRE ATT&amp;CK, with proof that it fires. HTB hasn't published the pass mark.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Four parts:</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 2" foreground="#0098a3">Methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your methodology, as numbered blank phases that you name and fill in your own way.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 13" foreground="#0098a3">Modules</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your notes, one per Academy module, in course order. Your methodology links back to these.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 280" foreground="#0098a3">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your exam workspace, with hosts, data sources, techniques, detection rules, the storyline, flags and a log for each day, laid out like the report.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="webs https://cnmoseman.github.io/htb-study-trackers/cdep/tracker/" foreground="#0098a3">CDEP Study Tracker</rich_text>
<rich_text>: the day-by-day study plan for this cert. Check off tasks there as you go.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#d9822b">Read this first
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Nobody has published a CDEP exam write-up yet, but HTB's report template is out. For each technique in the path, practice the write-up it asks for: how the behavior works, its ATT&amp;CK mapping, where its detections sit on the Summiting the Pyramid tables, and an SPL rule with proof it fires.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#2f9e44">Do the reporting module
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Do the </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://academy.hackthebox.com/course/preview/documentation--reporting" foreground="#0098a3">Documentation &amp; Reporting</rich_text>
<rich_text> module from the Penetration Tester path before your exam, even though it isn't in the CDEP path. It shows you how to take notes during an engagement and turn them into the kind of report HTB grades. It's built around the CPTS report, so it won't match the CDEP report one for one. Take the general tips and good habits from it and apply them to the CDEP report template.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">How to use it</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>1. Work through the course in order. As you finish each module, fill in its note.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>2. Build your methodology as you go. Rename each </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#0098a3">Fill in</rich_text>
<rich_text> phase to a step in your own workflow, and add or delete phases as you need. For a new phase, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Methodology Phase</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>3. Fill each phase with your own checklist, commands and decision points, and link back to the module notes: select some text, pick </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Insert › Insert/Edit Link</rich_text>
<rich_text>, choose </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">To Node</rich_text>
<rich_text> and pick the note.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>4. Keep one node per tool and one per log source under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tools &amp; Log Sources</rich_text>
<rich_text>. For a new one, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Tool</rich_text>
<rich_text> or </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Log Source</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tools &amp; Log Sources</rich_text>
<rich_text>. </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 278" foreground="#0098a3">WinDbg</rich_text>
<rich_text> and </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 279" foreground="#0098a3">ETW</rich_text>
<rich_text> are there to start you off. Link them from your module notes and phases so the commands you use most are one click away.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>5. Each module has one child node per Academy section. Expand a module in the tree to see its sections.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>6. On exam day, start at </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 280" foreground="#0098a3">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> and work from your methodology. The main nodes are in the </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Bookmarks</rich_text>
<rich_text> menu. Click any link to jump to the node behind it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Command sources</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Nobody has published CDEP cheat sheets yet. I'm watching for them and will add them here as they come out. Know of one? </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://github.com/cnmoseman/htb-study-trackers/issues/new?template=suggest-resource.yml&amp;cert=CDEP&amp;where=Prep+notes+%28command+sources%29&amp;title=%5BResource%5D+%5BCDEP%5D+" foreground="#0098a3">Suggest it on GitHub</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>Reporting: </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://docs.sysreptor.com/assets/reports/HTB-CDEP-Report.pdf" foreground="#0098a3">HTB CDEP report template</rich_text>
<rich_text> + </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://academy.hackthebox.com/course/preview/documentation--reporting" foreground="#0098a3">Documentation &amp; Reporting module</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">Made by</rich_text>
<rich_text> </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://github.com/cnmoseman" foreground="#0098a3">cnmoseman</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://cnmoseman.github.io/htb-study-trackers/" foreground="#0098a3">All HTB Study Trackers</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://github.com/cnmoseman/htb-study-trackers/issues/new?template=report-problem.yml&amp;cert=CDEP&amp;where=Prep+notes&amp;title=%5BProblem%5D+%5BCDEP%5D+" foreground="#0098a3">Report a problem</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<encoded_png char_offset="0" justification="left" link=""></encoded_png>
