<node name="ETW" unique_id="279" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cdep log-source" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">At a glance
</rich_text>
<rich_text>What it is: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Event Tracing for Windows, the kernel and user-mode event feed</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Searched in: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Your sensor or SIEM</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Learned in: </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 251" foreground="#0098a3">M13 - Windows Kernel Telemetry &amp; Detection Techniques</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Usual tools: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" link="node 278" foreground="#0098a3">WinDbg</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">, SilkETW</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">First Look</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">the first queries you run against it</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Checklist</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Which hosts send it, and to which index</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Time range it covers</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Key event IDs or fields noted</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Gaps and noise noted</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Useful queries saved to </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 285" foreground="#0098a3">Detection Rules</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Red Flags</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">things that usually mean a way forward</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Queries by Goal</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">one heading per thing you want from it</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h3" weight="heavy" style="italic">e.g. Watch one provider's events</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Notes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Queries</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Gotchas / Lessons Learned</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Links</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>Used in: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">link the methodology phase(s)</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>Tools: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" link="node 278" foreground="#0098a3">WinDbg</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>Index: </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 13" foreground="#0098a3">Modules</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<codebox char_offset="279" justification="left" frame_width="100" frame_height="74" width_in_pixels="0" syntax_highlighting="text" highlight_brackets="1" show_line_numbers="0"># query              # what it shows</codebox>
<table char_offset="504" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="240,240,240"><row><cell>e.g. A process opening another process with full access</cell><cell>e.g. Common before injection or credential theft</cell><cell>e.g. Check which process did it and why</cell></row><row><cell>What you see</cell><cell>Why it matters</cell><cell>Next step</cell></row></table>
<codebox char_offset="614" justification="left" frame_width="100" frame_height="74" width_in_pixels="0" syntax_highlighting="text" highlight_brackets="1" show_line_numbers="0"># query              # what it shows</codebox>
</node>
</node>
<node name="Exam" unique_id="280" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="#0098a3" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h1" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Your workspace for exam days: hosts, data sources, techniques, detection rules, the storyline, flags and a log for each day. Every table here matches a part of the </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://docs.sysreptor.com/assets/reports/HTB-CDEP-Report.pdf" foreground="#0098a3">official CDEP report template</rich_text>
<rich_text>, so by the end most of the report is already written down.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">The job
</rich_text>
<rich_text>The incident is already contained. Your job is to build the detections that would have caught each stage and prove each one works against the captured telemetry. HTB's loop for every task:</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>1. </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Characterize</rich_text>
<rich_text> the behavior, from the recovered sample or the telemetry, so the rule targets behavior, not a hash or filename.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>2. </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Map</rich_text>
<rich_text> it to the ATT&amp;CK technique or sub-technique.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>3. </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Author</rich_text>
<rich_text> the analytic over the right data source (Sysmon, the relevant ETW provider, ETW-TI, Security or auditd).</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>4. </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Validate</rich_text>
<rich_text> it on the captured corpus and confirm it fires on the true positive.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>5. </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Submit</rich_text>
<rich_text> the field value it returns. That value is the flag.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>HTB's template describes the example breach as five machines: a domain controller, three Windows workstations and a Linux build server.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Build your ATT&amp;CK Navigator layer as you go. The report attaches it as a JSON file.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#e03131">Keep this file private
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Once you start the exam, this file holds exam content. Don't push it to a public GitHub repo or share it, during or after the exam. HTB's terms don't allow it. To lock it with a password, use </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">File › Save As</rich_text>
<rich_text> and pick a </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Password Protected</rich_text>
<rich_text> storage type (</rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#0098a3">.ctx</rich_text>
<rich_text> or </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#0098a3">.ctz</rich_text>
<rich_text>).</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Start here</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>1. </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 281" foreground="#0098a3">01 - Before You Start</rich_text>
<rich_text>: go through the checklist before you start.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>2. </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 282" foreground="#0098a3">02 - Scope &amp; Rules</rich_text>
<rich_text>: copy the scope from the letter of engagement.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>3. Keep a log as you work: </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Log</rich_text>
<rich_text> has one node per exam day, from </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 291" foreground="#0098a3">Day 01</rich_text>
<rich_text> to </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 300" foreground="#0098a3">Day 10</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Hosts</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>One node per item under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Hosts</rich_text>
<rich_text>. Start with </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 289" foreground="#0098a3">Host 1</rich_text>
<rich_text> and rename it. For each new one, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Host</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Hosts</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Tracking</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 283" foreground="#0098a3">03 - Data Sources</rich_text>
<rich_text>: every telemetry source you rely on: Splunk index, sourcetype, key fields and gaps. Report: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Telemetry and Data Sources Used</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 284" foreground="#0098a3">04 - Techniques</rich_text>
<rich_text>: every technique you cover, with its hosts, time window and detection coverage. Report: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Identified Techniques Overview</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 285" foreground="#0098a3">05 - Detection Rules</rich_text>
<rich_text>: every SPL rule, whether it fired on the true positive, and its false positives. Report: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Proposed Detection Rules &amp; Correlations</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 286" foreground="#0098a3">06 - Storyline</rich_text>
<rich_text>: what the attacker did on each host, in time order. Report: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Cross-Host Detection Storyline</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 287" foreground="#0098a3">07 - Flags</rich_text>
<rich_text>: every flag and the rule that returned it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#0098a3">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<encoded_png char_offset="0" justification="left" link=""></encoded_png>
<node name="01 - Before You Start" unique_id="281" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cdep exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Setup</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>VPN connects and you can open Splunk</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Screenshot tool ready (Flameshot or similar). Paste each screenshot straight into the host's node with </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#0098a3">Ctrl+V</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Screenshot names picked, like </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#0098a3">ws01-t1197-rule1-fires.png</rich_text>
<rich_text> (item, step, what it shows), so you can find each one when you write the report</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Somewhere to save every query, its results and the proof it fired</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Report started from the HTB CDEP template in SysReptor</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>ATT&amp;CK Navigator open with a new layer to fill as you go. The report attaches it as a JSON file</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>WinDbg ready, for any trace files you analyze</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Autosave and backups on: </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">File › Preferences › Miscellaneous</rich_text>
<rich_text>, tick </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Autosave Every x Minutes</rich_text>
<rich_text> and </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Create a Backup Copy Before Saving</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>A copy of this file kept somewhere private. Only open it in one CherryTree window at a time, or you can lose changes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Read</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Letter of engagement read twice, scope copied into </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 282" foreground="#0098a3">02 - Scope &amp; Rules</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Exam start time, end time and report deadline written down</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>What counts as a flag and how to submit it</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Plan</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Rough plan for each day, with real breaks</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Sleep plan. Long exams are lost to fatigue more often than to missing skills.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Wordlists and tools ready on your attack box</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 280" foreground="#0098a3">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#0098a3">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
</node>
<node name="02 - Scope &amp; Rules" unique_id="282" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cdep exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">In Scope Assets</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">copy these from the letter of engagement; the report has the same table</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Out of Scope</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. A host the letter says not to touch</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Time Window</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">the report needs the exact start and end with the timezone; your event order and correlations depend on it</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Rules of Engagement</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. No denial of service</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Timeline</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 280" foreground="#0098a3">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#0098a3">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<table char_offset="88" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="191,236"><row><cell>e.g. DC01</cell><cell>e.g. Domain controller</cell></row><row><cell>e.g. WS01</cell><cell>e.g. Windows workstation</cell></row><row><cell>e.g. WS02</cell><cell>e.g. Windows workstation</cell></row><row><cell>e.g. WS03</cell><cell>e.g. Windows workstation</cell></row><row><cell>e.g. BUILD01</cell><cell>e.g. Linux build server</cell></row><row><cell>Host/URL/IP Address</cell><cell>Description</cell></row></table>
<table char_offset="267" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="146,240"><row><cell>Analysis start</cell><cell>e.g. 2026-09-09 08:00:00 UTC</cell></row><row><cell>Analysis end</cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>Item</cell><cell>Value</cell></row></table>
<table char_offset="328" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="110,240"><row><cell>Exam start</cell><cell>e.g. 2026-11-01 09:00 UTC</cell></row><row><cell>Exam end</cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>Report due</cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>Item</cell><cell>Date and time</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="03 - Data Sources" unique_id="283" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cdep exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>List every telemetry source you author or validate a rule on, so the work is reproducible. The report's </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Telemetry and Data Sources Used</rich_text>
<rich_text> section needs where each one lives in Splunk, the fields you rely on and any gaps that lower your confidence.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">the template lists Sysmon, ETW providers, ETW-TI, Windows Security and Linux auditd</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 280" foreground="#0098a3">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#0098a3">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<table char_offset="247" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="91,111,146,183,183,183"><row><cell>e.g. Sysmon</cell><cell>e.g. the index</cell><cell>e.g. the sourcetype</cell><cell>e.g. Image, CommandLine, ParentImage</cell><cell>e.g. process creation (Event ID 1)</cell><cell>e.g. no Event ID 10 on one host</cell></row><row><cell>Data source</cell><cell>Splunk index</cell><cell>Sourcetype</cell><cell>Key fields</cell><cell>Used for</cell><cell>Gaps</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="04 - Techniques" unique_id="284" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cdep exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Detection coverage
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">High:</rich_text>
<rich_text> built on hard-to-change behavior or strong telemetry, and resilient to simple evasion.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Medium:</rich_text>
<rich_text> useful, but can be bypassed with moderate effort or is sensitive to the environment.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Low:</rich_text>
<rich_text> fragile or noisy. It relies mostly on easy-to-change indicators.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">one row per technique; this becomes the report's Identified Techniques Overview</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 280" foreground="#0098a3">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#0098a3">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<table char_offset="282" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="110,101,200,240,236"><row><cell>e.g. F-001</cell><cell>e.g. WS01</cell><cell>e.g. T1197 BITS Jobs</cell><cell>e.g. 2026-09-09 10:14 to 10:20</cell><cell>e.g. High, Medium or Low</cell></row><row><cell>Finding ID</cell><cell>Host(s)</cell><cell>ATT&amp;CK technique</cell><cell>Time window (UTC)</cell><cell>Detection coverage</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="05 - Detection Rules" unique_id="285" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cdep exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>Only ship rules you've proven fire on the true positive. The full SPL and its proof sit in the host note, under its technique. This is the overview.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">the report shows each rule's output as a screenshot or table, and aims high on the Pyramid of Pain</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 280" foreground="#0098a3">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#0098a3">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<table char_offset="150" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="167,76,70,83,167,167,167"><row><cell>e.g. Rule 1: BITS job downloads a payload</cell><cell>e.g. T1197</cell><cell>e.g. WS01</cell><cell>e.g. Sysmon</cell><cell>e.g. yes, screenshot saved</cell><cell>e.g. admin software updates</cell><cell>e.g. the value it returned</cell></row><row><cell>Rule</cell><cell>Technique</cell><cell>Host</cell><cell>Data source</cell><cell>Fires on the true positive</cell><cell>False positives</cell><cell>Flag value</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="06 - Storyline" unique_id="286" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cdep exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>Rebuild the intrusion in time order across every in-scope host, from initial access to the end. The report's </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Cross-Host Detection Storyline</rich_text>
<rich_text> has one table per host.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3" style="italic">e.g. WS01</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3" style="italic">e.g. DC01</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 280" foreground="#0098a3">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#0098a3">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<table char_offset="175" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="236,240"><row><cell>e.g. 2026-09-09 10:14:22</cell><cell>e.g. Spearphishing attachment opened (T1566.001)</cell></row><row><cell>Time (UTC)</cell><cell>Activity</cell></row></table>
<table char_offset="188" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="110,92"><row><cell>e.g.</cell><cell>e.g.</cell></row><row><cell>Time (UTC)</cell><cell>Activity</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="07 - Flags" unique_id="287" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cdep exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Flags
</rich_text>
<rich_text>HTB hasn't published the flag count or the pass mark. Each flag is the field value your validated rule returns, so log the rule next to it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">add rows as you find more</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 280" foreground="#0098a3">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#0098a3">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<table char_offset="147" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="70,70,101,146,110"><row><cell>1</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>2</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>3</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>4</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>5</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>#</cell><cell>Host</cell><cell>Technique</cell><cell>Detection Rule</cell><cell>Flag Value</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="Hosts" unique_id="288" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="#0098a3" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>One node per item. Start with </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 289" foreground="#0098a3">Host 1</rich_text>
<rich_text> and rename it. For each new one, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Host</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Hosts</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<node name="Host 1" unique_id="289" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cdep host" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">At a glance
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Role: what the host does, like a workstation, the domain controller or a Linux build server. Status: todo, analyzing, validated or done.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Techniques go in </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 284" foreground="#0098a3">Techniques</rich_text>
<rich_text>, rules in </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 285" foreground="#0098a3">Detection Rules</rich_text>
<rich_text>, flags in </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 287" foreground="#0098a3">Flags</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Detection Engineering Synthesis</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">ATT&amp;CK-mapped summary of what happened on this host, and the coverage you can build and validate here</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. certutil (S0160) pulled down Rubeus (T1105), which ran AS-REP roasting (T1558.004)</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Next Up</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">what to work on next; tick it off as you go</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Validate a rule for the AS-REP roasting step</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Techniques</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">one section per technique, in the order the attacker used them; copy this whole section for each</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h3" weight="heavy" style="italic">e.g. BITS Jobs - T1197</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Detection Objective</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">why the attacker used it here and what it gave them</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Pulled the next-stage payload down without a browser</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Behavioral Breakdown</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">how it works, from the recovered sample and/or the telemetry, and how it links to the steps before and after</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tool / Tradecraft Analysis</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">a public tool? break down how it works and its choke points and invariants</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Artifact Analysis</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">capability analysis of a recovered sample, step by step; add your WinDbg trace analysis here if you used one</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Summiting the Pyramid: Host-Based Model</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">where each detection opportunity sits; aim for the higher rows</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Summiting the Pyramid: Network-Based Model</rich_text>
<rich_text> (if it applies)</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">ATT&amp;CK Detection Guidance</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. DET0098 - Detect abuse of Windows BITS Jobs</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Detection Rule 1:</rich_text>
<rich_text> </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. what it catches</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>Fires on the true positive: </rich_text>
