<node name="Host" unique_id="303" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cdep host" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">At a glance
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Role: what the host does, like a workstation, the domain controller or a Linux build server. Status: todo, analyzing, validated or done.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Techniques go in </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 284" foreground="#0098a3">Techniques</rich_text>
<rich_text>, rules in </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 285" foreground="#0098a3">Detection Rules</rich_text>
<rich_text>, flags in </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 287" foreground="#0098a3">Flags</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Detection Engineering Synthesis</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">ATT&amp;CK-mapped summary of what happened on this host, and the coverage you can build and validate here</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. certutil (S0160) pulled down Rubeus (T1105), which ran AS-REP roasting (T1558.004)</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Next Up</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">what to work on next; tick it off as you go</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Validate a rule for the AS-REP roasting step</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Techniques</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">one section per technique, in the order the attacker used them; copy this whole section for each</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h3" weight="heavy" style="italic">e.g. BITS Jobs - T1197</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Detection Objective</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">why the attacker used it here and what it gave them</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Pulled the next-stage payload down without a browser</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Behavioral Breakdown</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">how it works, from the recovered sample and/or the telemetry, and how it links to the steps before and after</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tool / Tradecraft Analysis</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">a public tool? break down how it works and its choke points and invariants</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Artifact Analysis</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">capability analysis of a recovered sample, step by step; add your WinDbg trace analysis here if you used one</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Summiting the Pyramid: Host-Based Model</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">where each detection opportunity sits; aim for the higher rows</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Summiting the Pyramid: Network-Based Model</rich_text>
<rich_text> (if it applies)</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">ATT&amp;CK Detection Guidance</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. DET0098 - Detect abuse of Windows BITS Jobs</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Detection Rule 1:</rich_text>
<rich_text> </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. what it catches</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>Fires on the true positive: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. yes, screenshot ws01-t1197-rule1-fires.png</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>False positives: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. admin software updates</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Additional Telemetry &amp; Detection Opportunities</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">missing telemetry, Sigma or YARA rules, API hook points worth intercepting</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Storyline</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">what happened on this host in time order; it feeds the Storyline note</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#0098a3">Related Modules</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" link="node 14" foreground="#0098a3">M01 - Detection &amp; OpSec Cyber Range</rich_text>
